{"path":"container/inplace_vector/reserve","title":"std::inplace_vector<T,N>::reserve","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::inplace_vector&lt;T,N&gt;::</span>reserve","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/reserve","section":"container","kind":"page","summary":"Does nothing, except that may throw std::bad_alloc. The request to increase the capacity (i.e., the internal storage size) is ignored because std::inplace_vector<T, N> is a fixed-capacity container.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx26\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">static</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span> reserve<span class=\"br0\">(</span> size_type new_cap <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Does nothing, except that may throw <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\">std::bad_alloc</a></span>. The request to increase the capacity (i.e., the internal storage size) is ignored because <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector\"><span class=\"kw3363\">std::<span class=\"me2\">inplace_vector</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, N<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span> is a fixed-capacity container.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> new_cap\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> new capacity of the <code>inplace_vector</code>, in number of elements\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Constant.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\">std::bad_alloc</a></span> if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">new_cap <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> capacity<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This function exists for compatibility with vector-like interfaces.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cassert&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;inplace_vector&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector\"><span class=\"kw3363\">std::<span class=\"me2\">inplace_vector</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">4</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> v<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw778\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>v.<span class=\"me1\">capacity</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">4</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> v.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    v.<span class=\"me1\">reserve</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// does nothing</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw778\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>v.<span class=\"me1\">capacity</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">4</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> v.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">try</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        v.<span class=\"me1\">reserve</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">13</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// throws, because requested capacity &gt; N; v is left unchanged</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">catch</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\"><span class=\"kw698\">std::<span class=\"me2\">bad_alloc</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> ex<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> ex.<span class=\"me1\">what</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw778\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>v.<span class=\"me1\">capacity</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">4</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> v.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>std::bad_alloc</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/size\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>size</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the number of elements <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/max_size\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>max_size</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the maximum possible number of elements <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/resize\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>resize</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  changes the number of elements stored <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/capacity\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>capacity</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the number of elements that can be held in currently allocated storage <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector/shrink_to_fit\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>shrink_to_fit</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  reduces memory usage by freeing unused memory <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"container","title":"Containers library"},{"path":"container/inplace_vector","title":"std::inplace_vector"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::inplace_vector<T,N>::reserve","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++26. Does nothing, except that may throw std::bad_alloc."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"new_cap"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Constant."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"std::bad_alloc if new_cap > capacity() is true."},{"label":"Notes","note":"This function exists for compatibility with vector-like interfaces."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"size","note":"returns the number of elements"},{"label":"max_size","note":"returns the maximum possible number of elements"},{"label":"resize","note":"changes the number of elements stored"},{"label":"capacity","note":"returns the number of elements that can be held in currently allocated storage"},{"label":"shrink_to_fit","note":"reduces memory usage by freeing unused memory"}]}]},"standards":["C++26"],"wordCount":202,"codeBlockCount":2}
